Package: doctor7-demo
Version: @VERSION@
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: doctor7-api, adduser, systemd
Maintainer: doctor7-onprem maintainers <maintainers@example.org>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://example.org/doctor7-onprem
Description: doctor7-onprem demo sign-in provider (demo only, never production)
 Mock identity provider for the public demo instance. It lists synthetic
 accounts, needs no password, and signs tokens with a key that exists only in
 memory. It is not a secure identity provider.
 .
 Demo only. Do not install this package on a production server. The package
 does not enable or start the service. An administrator does that on the demo
 host, after it fills in /etc/doctor7/idp-demo.env. The provider runs with the
 Node.js that doctor7-api finds: NODE_BIN, /opt/node/current/bin/node, or node
 from PATH. It must be version 22 or later.
